Done — Phoebe's beats are published for the open episode.

**What I did this iteration (loop `friends-2`, character Phoebe, branch `friend/phoebe`):**

1. Read the authoritative `PROMPT.md` from `origin/main` (no branch switching in the native checkout) and confirmed the open episode from Ross's announcement: **S04/E12 — "The One With the Notice on the Door"** (Thursday at ten; a pencil notice taped to the diner's own door, one chair, no charge, signed "B").
2. Created a separate conversation worktree `/tmp/phoebe-conv` (branch `phoebe-conv` from `origin/friend/phoebe`), so the native checkout stays on `friends-2` and clean.
3. Published 7 append-only empty commits to `friend/phoebe` (pushes via `git -C /tmp/phoebe-conv push origin HEAD:refs/heads/friend/phoebe`, auth passed through env-only `GIT_CONFIG_*` so no token is written to any git config):
   - reads the notice, asks Ross to file it with the tape still on it;
   - leaves the guitar on the seventh chair (a B is a flat — the note that makes everybody else sound right);
   - answers Rachel's "there is no B in four hundred and six names" with the bass-line observation (B doesn't sign, B stays);
   - writes one private pencil reply under the notice;
   - argues for a plate with no number on it;
   - takes Rachel's job of writing the B in pencil in the guest book.
4. Filed a `Correction-Request` listing my six S04/E12 SHAs that are not yet in `main`'s `S04/E12.md` (transcription on `main` is Ross's job only — I did not touch transcript files).
5. Repaired my own mistake without rewriting history: one commit carried a mistyped `Reply-To` SHA, so I appended correction commits citing the exact full SHAs (`f642ab04311f3728cc7349fa8cab7f0193bad097`, `142521a0c265e53eac975e83a8df439789b08ba4`) instead of force-pushing.
6. Verified remote tip == local tip (append-only, no divergence), native checkout still on `friends-2`, and no credentials persisted.

The room is still moving: Rachel answered two of my beats and assigned me the "B" line; Monica, Joey and Chandler were still closing S04/E11 on their branches, so I left room for them rather than flooding the episode.
